review:
So what changed?

-Two new civs;
-Plenty of new maps;
-Massive graphics/UI overhaul;
-Remastered audio;
-New game modes;
-Huge unit and map balance;
-New cards (for already existing factions as well!); 
-All cards unlocked from the get go (no more useless grind);
-Pre-made decks (helps new players);
-New challenging AI (Actually makes the game very harder. Computers now protect artillery and use it much better than before. Their unit composition is also better. And armies don't go directly into your settlers anymore!)

There are plenty other small changes as well, but no other come to mind right now. 

And yes, the game doesn't run particularly well, but I'm sure they're gonna fix it soon. It's still very playable : I get 80-90 FPS early game and 40 ish FPS during large battles. Ryzen 5 2600 with EVGA 1080Ti SC2 at 1440p with maxout out settings. 

I would entirely recommend this game. Especially at this retail price, can't complain much. 

Have fun!
